    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1037">

                <pb facs="1080" n="1068" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1068"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/5–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-06T21:00:00+02:00">May 6, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 6—8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2425. ReEmbtel 2381, May 5, 1 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d1037-f1"/> Duff Cooper
                    tells me that de Gaulle promised him last night to turn over one brigade of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Troupes Spéciales</hi> to the Syrians in the very
                    near future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
